    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0534" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.014 Bessarabia/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-29T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1866. Mission. Bessarabian treaty was signed October 28th by Cambon, Derby,
                        Jonesco,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d507-f1"/> and Ghika.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d507-f2"/> Ishii being at Brussels, treaty was left open for his
                        signature<anchor n="10" xml:id="d507-f3"/> as well [as] for those of British
                    Dominions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d507-f1" n="8" xml:id="d507-f1-content">
                <p>Take Jonesco, Rumanian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d507-f2" n="9" xml:id="d507-f2-content">
                <p>Prince Dimitrie Ghika, Rumanian Minister to France.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d507-f3" n="10" xml:id="d507-f3-content">
                <p>Viscount Ishii signed on Oct. 30.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
